INSERT INTO `employment` VALUES ('0597d3af-253d-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','NineMSN Pty Ltd (A Microsoft Company)','Internet Programmer','236d1f34-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','1998-02-08','1998-08-28','NineMSN (a child company of Microsoft and the Channel 9 Network) was my baptism into ASP and the last job I had before leaving Australia. I worked on many sites for them including Getaway Travel (the Australian forerunner to Expedia), Money (a web version of the print publication), Dolly Magazine, Wine Society Magazine and Telstra Big Pond (Australia\'s premier phone company). I also designed and developed various temporary, interstitial and redirectional pages to maintain company image and attract advertisers.'),('08dd881b-7c79-44ca-8f77-34a8b066ddd9','Internet.au Magazine (Next Publishing)','Technical Journalist','236d1f34-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','1998-08-31','1999-05-31','This was the last job that I did for an Australian company. While working at NextData I moonlighted by writing articles for the Australian publication which included a feature article on, what at the time was the latest technology: ASP-VBScript. I also wrote a five part series of articles instructing beginners on Sun\'s Java Development Kit (to version 1.2). This led to a regular monthly Question and Answer column which I designed and developed a website specifically for.'),('08dd8c01-7535-4468-8686-562ab12bb6b4','Widget Incorporated','Contract Programmer / CTO','236d26c8-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2006-05-27','2015-08-04','At various times in my career I have worked as a freelance contractor under the banner of Widget Incorporated. Clients that I\'ve helped out in various capacities as IT support under Widget include:\n\nMountainpeek Creations (quilting supplies)\nAfrica Adventure Consultants (African tours)\nRack and Roll (clothing boutique)\nFoley Entertainment (music industry)\n3NE Records (music industry)\nFyrewerks (fire prevention)\nDan Pabon for HD4 (political candidate)\nLodo Toastmasters (local chapter of Toastmasters International)\nArapahoe Community College (where I now study)\nThe Merisol Group (oil and gas)\nInternet Information Systems Services Group (employment agency)\nHeritage Hotels (hotel chain)'),('08dd8c01-e64b-4fdf-8579-3a3a79f71d6e','NexData Solutions','Senior Internet Application Design Specialist','236d28e4-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','1999-08-27','2000-02-29','When the department manager at NexData Solutions took a position at PartMiner Incorporated, he asked me to come along. In my time at NexData I had been a technical lead on a New York trip with the sales team and was instrumental in landing a major contract for the development of the corporate e-commerce web site for the Langenscheidt book publishing firm. In addition, I designed the site. I left before development began, however, but I did design and create the company Intranet system.'),('08dd8c02-17ca-4f5c-85a3-9e8b61773343','PartMiner Incorporated ‐ Englewood, CO','Senior Software Engineer','236d295d-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2000-02-29','2001-02-27','It was mostly my experience at PartMiner Inc. which got me the job at CapitalIQ but when I was with PartMiner there was no WebQL. Despite the limitations of the technology at the time, I still created an Internet \"mining\" tool to analyze web sites and extract information for increased productivity, using Java / J2EE.\n\nWhile I was there I also designed and developed an Internet information extractor to maintain the company database of marketable information using the now-primative Delphi 5 as well as a recursive Internet mining and extraction program for increased productivity and intelligence using Visual Basic 6.0.\n\nEven at this early stage in my career I was involved in leadership activities as I trained co-workers in ASP, Java and JavaScript as technical backups. ASP, in particular, was a fairly new technology and I was glad that I could use the skills from my defunct teaching career in this effort.'),('08dd8c02-6733-4b1b-823c-171ed9237f2f','Eagle:XM (formerly EagleDirect Marketing)','Software Developer / Project Manager','236d26c8-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2002-12-31','2006-05-31','I was with Eagle:XM for three and a half years, supporting and enhancing their flagship \"Broadband Insights\" product for delivering statistical information of users for various cable television companies. This information was considered critical to their marketing strategy. By targetting direct mailings to a statistically more inclined audience, Eagle:XM boasted a return three times higher than other direct marketing companies.\n\nI also helped to keep them on the cutting edge of technology by designing and developing various in-house tools including the main data warehouse to replace the existing DOS based system.'),('08dd8c02-8bf1-46b2-87d3-17df783d44aa','OnCommand Corporation','Software Developer','236d26c8-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2006-05-31','2006-12-31','I have two achievements at OnCommand (later LodgeNet and now Sonifi). One was designing and developing their primary database analysis and viewing tools, thus reducing costs in licensing fees for their existing systems.\n\nThe other was designing and developing their in-house project management intranet system in order to streamline their project development lifecycle; a project which has contributed greatly to my software development project management experience.\n\nIn addition I was involved in support programming for their existing hotel network analysis and updating tools.'),('08dd8c02-bcaa-473c-834c-4bedcfde2f3f','Capital IQ (A division of Standards & Poors)','Web Mining Developer','236d29c3-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2006-12-31','2007-12-31','Along with support programming and script development for their web mining operation, I designed and developed their Document Feed service to expedite the delivery of web mined documents to their client companies. In addition, I was heavily involved in creating various scripts using (the very obscure) WebQL technology for analyzing web sites and identifying and downloading relevant documents pertaining to the financial sector. This was of particular interest to the parent company, Standards & Poors.'),('08dd8c02-dd91-4f5e-8714-b5219eaef03d','Kinder Morgan','Intranet Developer','236d27dc-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2007-12-31','2008-12-31','I designed and developed four major intranet systems for Kinder Morgan: fleet management, action auditing, equipment inspection and waste management. Ask me about any of these or any of the other ones that you may see on my website!'),('08dd8c03-0407-441c-8290-dc699c5e4ed8','Global Healthcare Exchange','Web Applications Developer','236d2a25-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2008-12-31','2009-05-31','I added functionality to their Internet and Intranet systems in order to track the sales of medical supplies for their clients. This enabled them to analyze this information in more detail for marketing purposes.'),('08dd8c03-2a4a-4d7f-8b5f-b7c14f59919d','Aspire Financial Services','Lead Developer','236d27dc-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2009-05-31','2009-12-31','Along with an offshore team based in India which I managed, I helped to update the company infrastructure from its proprietary, legacy VB6 version to .NET technology utilizing C#, VB.NET and MVC.'),('08dd8c03-4c0c-4939-8fae-ac88b51a6b37','FIMAC Solutions','Software Consultant','236d286f-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2009-12-31','2011-12-31','I added value to the company by designing and developing the web-based version of their flagship budget modelling product.\n\nBefore modern frameworks, I bolstered their development capabilities by creating a custom php framework and all visual components including treeviews, drag and drop operations and ajax-updated tables and table cells.\n\nTo support these efforts I also designed and developed complex SQL queries for data retrieval to populated ajax enabled data tables.\n\nAnd, before jQuery, React or Angular (which I have since been using), I developed all of the native javascript routines for client-side visual effects including fade in / out, dynamic resizing and conditional data ajax retrieval (ie: retrieving treeview data as needed utilizing ajax functionality)'),('08dd8c03-864b-4665-89a2-07d7ee5afc12','United States Department of the Interior','Contract Programmer','236d27dc-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2014-05-31','2015-05-31','For internal efficiency, I designed and developed an internal Cloud Services request intranet system including email forwarding and custom content management.\n\nI also designed and developed a catalog intranet system for employee self-service, helping to reduce tech support load.\n\nIn addition, I designed and developed web services using the latest Java Development Kit for communications with a MySQL database for added security for the aforementioned internal web applications.\n\nTo increase convenience and security, I incorporated a SimpleSAMLphp interface for single sign-on to their internal web applications as well as set up and administered a Linux Apache hosting system.'),('08dd8c05-a8b5-43f6-875f-547634523192','PlanetEcosystems / Franklin Energy','Lead Developer','236d28e4-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2016-07-31','2018-03-31','In order to track customer usage to increasing sales, I installed and configured a Cassandra noSQL database\n\nFor the purpose of conforming to the industry standard, I was also instrumental by creating client services to export energy usage data to the Green Button XML data format.\n\nPerhaps my proudest achievement, I increased performance of the Equipment Marketplace section of their Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) website – the cornerstone of their company product – by 97% by redesigning and redeveloping the internal structure to increasing the efficiency of cataloging product information retrieved from APIs for Amazon (AWS), Best Buy, Sears, Shopping.com and ShopToIt.ca (for Canadian clients)'),('08dd8c05-dd4f-4ff7-823f-d265780a51d7','LB Media Group, LLC.','Director of Software Development','236d286f-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2018-03-31','2019-09-30','As Lead Developer I was responsible for the overall design, development and maintainence the internal Account Management System which is used to track clients, sales and payments.\n\nAs Director of Software Development I was given the additional responsibility of overseeing and maintaining the newly acquired Greenlight website.'),('08dd8c06-19ef-48b7-8fc0-047dca1a2503','Colorado Secretary of State','Contract Programmer','236d26c8-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2020-04-30','2020-12-31','I was mainly engaged in increasing the efficiency of their public self-service websites by analyzing and debugging legacy systems.\n\nI was also involved in the development of a replacement ballot request process component in preparation for the last election as well as adding features and enchancement to their notary registration website.'),('08dd8c06-57a4-406f-8e04-3f850218d387','Digital Intelligence Systems','Software Developer','236d27dc-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2021-02-28','2021-05-31','This was a fill-in project. My experience was utilized in a standard fashion, working with a team to produce an internal data system for our client, State Farm.'),('08dd8c06-8ae0-4d13-8e8a-9ccad5c9b6bc','Alius Health','Senior Software Developer / Team Lead','236d2a8a-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2021-05-31','2022-01-31','I was involved in some development work, refreshing my dormant C# programming skills, as well as designing a document management system. I also streamlined their production release cycle and data import using a product called ArcESB.\n\nPerhaps my best achievement at Alius was organizing two projects through their entire lifecycle, from initial design to deployment. I was responsible for creating and assigning the tasks in GIT.\n\nI also acted as Team Lead, implementing a weekly developers’ meeting that turned out to be a very successful forum by providing a forum for the programmers to find solutions to problems, both technical and political. I was able to utilize my Toastmasters skills by providing a buffer between management and the guys in the trenches.'),('08dd8c06-eae4-47e2-87eb-073d31403fa8','Various Clients','Private Contractor','236d27dc-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2022-01-31','2024-06-30','Lead development teams for diverse clients, including PIN Business Network, PeopleCare Health Services, MITEC Fire Prevention Services, FIS Global for State Farm, and Colorado Secretary of State. Enhance e-commerce systems, healthcare software, and fire prevention service tracking through strategic planning and execution. Coordinated project management activities to ensure seamless development cycles and client satisfaction. Utilize advanced technologies such as C# .NET Core, SQL Server, and Docker for system architecture and deployment. Implement ongoing maintenance and updates for client systems, leveraging PHP, Java, and modern JavaScript frameworks like JavaScript (ECMAScript 6). Collaborate closely with stakeholders to deliver tailored software solutions that drive revenue growth and operational efficiency. Apply industry best practices and technological expertise to optimize system performance and enhance user experience across diverse platforms.\n●	Led a team of three developers to successfully deliver a robust e-commerce platform for PIN Business Network. This initiative significantly boosted revenue and market visibility for political materials.\n●	Managed a team of two developers at PeopleCare Health Services, overseeing the enhancement and maintenance of their personal care services software, crucial for delivering healthcare services.\n●	Ensured the seamless operation of MITEC Fire Prevention Services\' internal customer and services tracking system, utilizing PHP, JavaScript, and CSS to maintain up-to-date functionalities.\n●	Expanded and maintained FIS Global\'s internal customer tracking system for State Farm using Java, MySQL, JavaScript, and CSS.\n●	Developed enhancements for the voter registration system at Colorado Secretary of State, improving functionality for the 2000 General Election using Java, JSF, JSP, Spring, and JavaScript (ECMAScript 6) on WebSphere Application Server integrated with Jenkins Automation Server.\n'),('08dd8c07-1405-4a09-8087-22cb1b92dff1','Flatwater Inc.','Software Developer','236d27dc-253a-11f0-a7ca-dc454691e924','2024-06-30','2025-05-04','Participated in the design of an online system for the efficient utilization of land resources owned by the Native American community, in conjunction with the United States Bureau of Indian Affairs, to replace the existing desktop application. \nDesigned and developed a system for the migration of the existing Oracle database used by the desktop system, to SQL Server, including duplicating and modifying table structures for consistency and efficiency.\nOngoing work includes creating a series of APIs to securely retrieve data from the new SQL Server database system.\n\n');
